      "hints": [
        "Provide `chatInput` (and optionally `sessionId`) as run inputs; the original started from a chat message.",
        "\"Get All Files\": set the Supabase project ref (Management API) on SUPABASE_SELECT_ROWS.",
        "\"AI Agent\" used agent tools in the original: Vector Store Tool1 (toolVectorStore). The cdecli agent calls connectors directly; connect credentials for the services those tools reached.",
        "\"Get All files\" authenticated with supabaseApi in the original; add the matching Authorization header (or use the service's connector).",
        "\"Loop Over Items\" uses NodeLoop: process each item/batch, return through NEXT, and continue only after all results are collected.",
        "\"Download\" authenticated with supabaseApi in the original; add the matching Authorization header (or use the service's connector).",
        "\"Extract Document PDF\" (extractFromFile.pdf): Parsed via googlesuper/GOOGLESUPER_PARSE_FILE; the file must live on Google Drive (upload first if the previous step only has bytes/base64).",
        "\"Extract Document PDF\": GOOGLESUPER_PARSE_FILE needs a Drive file_id (and googlesuper credential). If the upstream step only has file bytes, upload with GOOGLESUPER_CREATE_FILE_FROM_TEXT / Drive upload first, then parse.",
        "\"Create File record2\": set the Supabase project ref (Management API) on SUPABASE_INSERT_ROW.",
        "\"Insert into Supabase Vectorstore\" folded a document (documentDefaultDataLoader); retrieved text is expected on the upstream payload as context/documents.",
        "\"Insert into Supabase Vectorstore\": set the Supabase project ref on SUPABASE_INSERT_ROW. content, embedding, and metadata come from the upstream item.",
        "Select the Project and Environment on the Workflow Configs node (the ids from `cdecli auth status`), then connect a credential for each connector below.",
        "Connect googlesuper: `cdecli credential create -n \"googlesuper\" -p googlesuper --template <formId> --secret <key>=<value>` (see `cdecli credential templates`).",
